<span id="S4.T1.2.1.1.1.5.7" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_center" style="padding:-0.4pt 2.0pt;"><span id="S4.T1.2.1.1.1.5.7.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">0.790</span> / <span id="S4.T1.2.1.1.1.5.7.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">618</span> / <span id="S4.T1.2.1.1.1.5.7.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">1.000</span></span></span>
<span id="S4.T1.2.1.1.1.6" class="ltx_tr">
<span id="S4.T1.2.1.1.1.6.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_bb" style="padding:-0.4pt 2.0pt;">RLOO</span>
<span id="S4.T1.2.1.1.1.6.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_border_bb" style="padding:-0.4pt 2.0pt;">0.827 / 677 / 0.965  <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:0.6pt;--ltx-fg-color:#A6A6A6;--ltx-bg-color:#A6A6A6;display:inline-block;"> </span></span>
<span id="S4.T1.2.1.1.1.6.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb" style="padding:-0.4pt 2.0pt;"><span id="S4.T1.2.1.1.1.6.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">0.829</span> / 813 / 0.940</span>
<span id="S4.T1.2.1.1.1.6.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_border_bb" style="padding:-0.4pt 2.0pt;">0.820 / 720 / 0.940  <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:0.6pt;--ltx-fg-color:#A6A6A6;--ltx-bg-color:#A6A6A6;display:inline-block;"> </span></span>
<span id="S4.T1.2.1.1.1.6.5" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb" style="padding:-0.4pt 2.0pt;"><span id="S4.T1.2.1.1.1.6.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">0.823</span> / <span id="S4.T1.2.1.1.1.6.5.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">639</span> / <span id="S4.T1.2.1.1.1.6.5.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">0.955</span></span>
<span id="S4.T1.2.1.1.1.6.6" class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_border_bb" style="padding:-0.4pt 2.0pt;">0.830 / 565 / 0.967  <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:0.6pt;--ltx-fg-color:#A6A6A6;--ltx-bg-color:#A6A6A6;display:inline-block;"> </span></span>
<span id="S4.T1.2.1.1.1.6.7" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb" style="padding:-0.4pt 2.0pt;"><span id="S4.T1.2.1.1.1.6.7.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">0.843</span> / 700 / <span id="S4.T1.2.1.1.1.6.7.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">0.980</span></span></span>
</span>
</span></span></p>
</span></div>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 1: </span>Pareto fronts obtained from hypervolume-guided weight adaptation compared to fixed-weight baselines. <math id="S4.T1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\uparrow" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo stretchy="false">↑</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\uparrow</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.T1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\downarrow" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo stretchy="false">↓</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\downarrow</annotation></semantics></math> indicate optimization direction. Each value represents the average performance across the entire Pareto front under a given training setup. <span id="S4.T1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Hypervolume-guided weighting outperforms baselines across most objectives, weight configurations, and RL algorithms</span>, and in certain cases, demonstrates full dominance with superior results on all three objectives.</figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="S4.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We compare our hypervolume-guided weight adaptation against fixed-weight baselines in <a href="#S4.T1" title="Table 1 ‣ 4.2 Results ‣ 4 Hypervolume-Guided Weight Adaptation ‣ Learning to Optimize Multi-Objective Alignment Through Dynamic Reward Weighting" class="ltx_ref ltx_refmacro_autoref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Table 1</span></a>. Across all three online RL algorithms, there is consistently at least one weight configuration where our method outperforms the baselines on all objectives. For example, under both accuracy- and efficiency-focused settings, REINFORCE equipped with hypervolume-guided weighting achieves Pareto fronts that have better average scores across all three objectives.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S4.F3" class="ltx_figure ltx_align_floatright" style="width:39%;"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2509.11452v1/meta_reward_distributions.svg" id="S4.F3.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:220/126;" width="220" height="126"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 3: </span>Meta-reward <math id="S4.F3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{\text{pareto}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>r</mi><mtext>pareto</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{\text{pareto}}</annotation></semantics></math> distributions, with vertical dashed lines indicating the average value.</figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="S4.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">It is important to note that better average scores of Pareto fronts do not necessarily guarantee true Pareto optimality. Due to space constraints, we include the full Pareto front visualizations in Appendix <a href="#A1.SS6" title="A.6 Pareto Fronts Visualization ‣ Appendix A Appendix ‣ Learning to Optimize Multi-Objective Alignment Through Dynamic Reward Weighting" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.6</span></a>. These plots provide compelling visual evidence that REINFORCE with our hypervolume-guided weight adaptation achieves clearly superior Pareto fronts, dominating baseline methods under both accuracy- and efficiency-focused settings. This visual analysis confirms and strengthens the quantitative results presented above.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS2.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.SS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">To better understand the performance differences between weight configurations, we analyze the meta-reward <math id="S4.SS2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{\text{pareto}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>r</mi><mtext>pareto</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{\text{pareto}}</annotation></semantics></math> during REINFORCE training. As shown in <a href="#S4.F3" title="Figure 3 ‣ 4.2 Results ‣ 4 Hypervolume-Guided Weight Adaptation ‣ Learning to Optimize Multi-Objective Alignment Through Dynamic Reward Weighting" class="ltx_ref ltx_refmacro_autoref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Figure 3</span></a>, the balanced weight setting yields higher meta-rewards that encourage more aggressive exploration, paradoxically, leading to suboptimal performance compared to two other configurations. This suggests that effective hypervolume-guided weighting requires careful calibration of meta-reward to avoid overly aggressive updates that can hinder convergence.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S5" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">5 </span>Gradient-Based Weight Optimization</h2>

<div id="S5.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We now consider a more sophisticated yet flexible setting where reward weights are not fixed but dynamically adapted in real-time. In this scenario, human-specified preferences are not assumed. We formulate the online weights adaptation during training as an optimization problem and begin our study with the natural policy-gradient method REINFORCE:</p>
<table id="S5.EGx2" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S5.E2"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.E2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\nabla J(\theta)=\mathbb{E}\!\big[\nabla\log\pi_{\theta}(a_{t}\mid s_{t})\,G^{w}_{t}\big]," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>J</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.497em;" width="0.497em"><mi>𝔼</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>log</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>G</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>w</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\nabla J(\theta)=\mathbb{E}\!\big[\nabla\log\pi_{\theta}(a_{t}\mid s_{t})\,G^{w}_{t}\big],</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(2)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.p1.2" class="ltx_p">which exhibits linearity to the per-objective gradients given by <math id="S5.p1.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\nabla J(\theta)=\sum_{i=1}^{K}w_{i}\,\nabla J_{i}(\theta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>J</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>K</mi></msubsup><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>J</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla J(\theta)=\sum_{i=1}^{K}w_{i}\,\nabla J_{i}(\theta)</annotation></semantics></math>. We prove this linearity through a simple nested summation <math id="S5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G^{w}_{t}=\sum_{l=0}^{\infty}\gamma^{l}r_{t+l+1}^{w}=\sum_{l=0}^{\infty}\gamma^{l}\sum_{i=1}^{K}w_{i}r_{t+l+1}^{i}=\sum_{i=1}^{K}w_{i}\sum_{l=0}^{\infty}\gamma^{l}r_{t+l+1}^{i}=\sum_{i=1}^{K}w_{i}G_{t}^{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>G</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>w</mi></msubsup><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msubsup><mrow><msup><mi>γ</mi><mi>l</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>r</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>l</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>w</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msubsup><mrow><msup><mi>γ</mi><mi>l</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>K</mi></msubsup><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>r</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>l</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>i</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>K</mi></msubsup><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msubsup><mrow><msup><mi>γ</mi><mi>l</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>r</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>l</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>i</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>K</mi></msubsup><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>G</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G^{w}_{t}=\sum_{l=0}^{\infty}\gamma^{l}r_{t+l+1}^{w}=\sum_{l=0}^{\infty}\gamma^{l}\sum_{i=1}^{K}w_{i}r_{t+l+1}^{i}=\sum_{i=1}^{K}w_{i}\sum_{l=0}^{\infty}\gamma^{l}r_{t+l+1}^{i}=\sum_{i=1}^{K}w_{i}G_{t}^{i}</annotation></semantics></math>. Then there exists a constant <math id="S5.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C\in\mathbb{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C\in\mathbb{R}</annotation></semantics></math> such that <math id="S5.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J(\theta)=\sum_{i=1}^{K}w_{i}J_{i}(\theta)+C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>K</mi></msubsup><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>J</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J(\theta)=\sum_{i=1}^{K}w_{i}J_{i}(\theta)+C</annotation></semantics></math>, which implies</p>
<table id="S5.Ex4" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.Ex4.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\argmin_{{\bm{w}}\in\Delta^{K}}J(\theta({\bm{w}}))=\argmin_{{\bm{w}}\in\Delta^{K}}\sum_{i=1}^{K}w_{i}J_{i}(\theta)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mi>arg</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>min</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>𝐰</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>K</mi></msup></mrow></msub><mi>J</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐰</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mi>arg</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>min</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>𝐰</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>K</mi></msup></mrow></msub><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>K</mi></munderover><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><msub><mi>J</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\argmin_{{\bm{w}}\in\Delta^{K}}J(\theta({\bm{w}}))=\argmin_{{\bm{w}}\in\Delta^{K}}\sum_{i=1}^{K}w_{i}J_{i}(\theta)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.p1.3" class="ltx_p">Inspired by domain adaptation <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib9" title="" class="ltx_ref">Fan et al., 2024</a>)</cite> and based on the above linearity assumption, we can derive the following reward weight update rule, where <math id="S5.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>η</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta</annotation></semantics></math> is the learning rate and <math id="S5.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>μ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu</annotation></semantics></math> is the regularization factor (we provide full proof in Appendix <a href="#A1.SS1" title="A.1 Proof for Gradient-Based Weight Optimization ‣ Appendix A Appendix ‣ Learning to Optimize Multi-Objective Alignment Through Dynamic Reward Weighting" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.1</span></a> and the whole procedure in Algorithm <a href="#alg2" title="Algorithm 2 ‣ 5.2 Experiment Setup ‣ 5 Gradient-Based Weight Optimization ‣ Learning to Optimize Multi-Objective Alignment Through Dynamic Reward Weighting" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>):</p>
<table id="S5.EGx3" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S5.E3"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.E3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle{\bm{w}}^{(t)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝒘</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle{\bm{w}}^{(t)}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.E3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{{\bm{w}}^{(t)}}{\sum_{k}w_{k}^{(t)}},\quad\text{where}\;{\bm{w}}^{(t)}={\bm{w}}^{(t-1)}\odot\exp(\frac{\eta^{(t)}{\bm{I}}^{(t)}}{\mu}),I_{i}^{(t)}=\langle\nabla J_{i}(\theta^{(t)}),\sum_{k\in[K]}\nabla J_{k}(\theta^{(t)})\rangle." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mi>𝒘</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>k</mi></msub><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mi>k</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mtext>where</mtext><mo lspace="0.280em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝒘</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝒘</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊙</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>η</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝑰</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><mi>μ</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>I</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>J</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>J</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{{\bm{w}}^{(t)}}{\sum_{k}w_{k}^{(t)}},\quad\text{where}\;{\bm{w}}^{(t)}={\bm{w}}^{(t-1)}\odot\exp(\frac{\eta^{(t)}{\bm{I}}^{(t)}}{\mu}),I_{i}^{(t)}=\langle\nabla J_{i}(\theta^{(t)}),\sum_{k\in[K]}\nabla J_{k}(\theta^{(t)})\rangle.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(3)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="Thmremarkx1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_remark">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmremarkx1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Remark</span></span><span id="Thmremarkx1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmremarkx1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmremarkx1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The <math id="Thmremarkx1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I_{i}^{(t)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>I</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I_{i}^{(t)}</annotation></semantics></math> measures the total influence that learning objective <math id="Thmremarkx1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> has on the remaining <math id="Thmremarkx1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K-1</annotation></semantics></math> objectives (<math id="Thmremarkx1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\langle\nabla J_{i},\sum_{k\neq i}\nabla J_{k}\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>J</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>J</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\langle\nabla J_{i},\sum_{k\neq i}\nabla J_{k}\rangle</annotation></semantics></math>) plus the magnitude of its own gradient (<math id="Thmremarkx1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\nabla J_{i}\|_{2}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>J</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\nabla J_{i}\|_{2}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>). Intuitively, similar to prior studies in data influence <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib21" title="" class="ltx_ref">Koh &amp; Liang, 2017</a>)</cite> and domain adaptation <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib9" title="" class="ltx_ref">Fan et al., 2024</a>)</cite>, we upweight an objective when it has high learning potential on other objectives (high influence) and has not been learned enough yet (high gradient magnitude).</p>
</div>
</div>
<section id="S5.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">5.1 </span>Convergence Analysis</h3>

<div id="S5.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S5.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">A natural concern in weight updating is whether the weights may collapse to zero or explode to the boundary value of one within a single update step. To address this concern, we provide a convergence analysis for Eq. <a href="#S5.E3" title="In 5 Gradient-Based Weight Optimization ‣ Learning to Optimize Multi-Objective Alignment Through Dynamic Reward Weighting" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>.
We first make some standard assumptions used across existing RL <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib41" title="" class="ltx_ref">Wang et al., 2017</a>; <a href="#bib.bib43" title="" class="ltx_ref">Wu et al., 2020</a>; <a href="#bib.bib22" title="" class="ltx_ref">Kumar et al., 2023</a>)</cite> and multi-objective optimization studies <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib55" title="" class="ltx_ref">Zhou et al., 2022</a>; <a href="#bib.bib27" title="" class="ltx_ref">Liu &amp; Vicente, 2024</a>; <a href="#bib.bib47" title="" class="ltx_ref">Xu et al., 2025</a>)</cite>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S5.Thmassumption1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_assumption">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S5.Thmassumption1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Assumption 5.1</span></span><span id="S5.Thmassumption1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Lipschitz Continuity)<span id="S5.Thmassumption1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S5.Thmassumption1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.Thmassumption1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.Thmassumption1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">The policy <math id="S5.Thmassumption1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\theta}</annotation></semantics></math> is differentiable with respect to <math id="S5.Thmassumption1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>θ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta</annotation></semantics></math> and the output <math id="S5.Thmassumption1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\log\pi_{\theta}(a\mid s)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\log\pi_{\theta}(a\mid s)</annotation></semantics></math> is L-Lipschitz and has bounded norm <math id="S5.Thmassumption1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\nabla\log\pi_{\theta}(a\mid s)\|\leq B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>log</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\nabla\log\pi_{\theta}(a\mid s)\|\leq B</annotation></semantics></math> for any <math id="S5.Thmassumption1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>θ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S5.Thmassumption2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_assumption">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S5.Thmassumption2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Assumption 5.2</span></span><span id="S5.Thmassumption2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Bounded Reward)<span id="S5.Thmassumption2.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S5.Thmassumption2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.Thmassumption2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.Thmassumption2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">The reward is bounded in the range <math id="S5.Thmassumption2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[0,r_{\text{max}}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">max</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[0,r_{\text{max}}]</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S5.Thmassumption3" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_assumption">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S5.Thmassumption3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Assumption 5.3</span></span><span id="S5.Thmassumption3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Learning Rate)<span id="S5.Thmassumption3.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S5.Thmassumption3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.Thmassumption3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.Thmassumption3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">The learning rate <math id="S5.Thmassumption3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta^{(t)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>η</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta^{(t)}</annotation></semantics></math> is non-increasing and non-negative.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S5.Thmassumption4" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_assumption">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S5.Thmassumption4.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Assumption 5.4</span></span><span id="S5.Thmassumption4.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Bounded Policy Gradient)<span id="S5.Thmassumption4.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S5.Thmassumption4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.Thmassumption4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.Thmassumption4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">The true gradient (Eq. <a href="#S5.E2" title="In 5 Gradient-Based Weight Optimization ‣ Learning to Optimize Multi-Objective Alignment Through Dynamic Reward Weighting" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>) of the objective function is bounded <math id="S5.Thmassumption4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\nabla J_{k}(\theta)\|\leq C\leq\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>J</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>C</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\nabla J_{k}(\theta)\|\leq C\leq\infty</annotation></semantics></math> which is established by <math id="S5.Thmassumption4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\nabla\log\pi_{\theta}(a\mid s)\|&lt;B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>log</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\nabla\log\pi_{\theta}(a\mid s)\|&lt;B</annotation></semantics></math> (Assumption <a href="#S5.Thmassumption1" title="Assumption 5.1 (Lipschitz Continuity). ‣ 5.1 Convergence Analysis ‣ 5 Gradient-Based Weight Optimization ‣ Learning to Optimize Multi-Objective Alignment Through Dynamic Reward Weighting" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.1</span></a>) and <math id="S5.Thmassumption4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{t}=\sum_{l=0}^{\infty}\gamma^{l}r_{t+l+1}\leq\sum_{l=0}^{\infty}\gamma^{l}r_{\text{max}}=\frac{r_{\text{max}}}{1-\gamma}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msubsup><mrow><msup><mi>γ</mi><mi>l</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>l</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">≤</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msubsup><mrow><msup><mi>γ</mi><mi>l</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">max</mtext></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>r</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">max</mtext></msub><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{t}=\sum_{l=0}^{\infty}\gamma^{l}r_{t+l+1}\leq\sum_{l=0}^{\infty}\gamma^{l}r_{\text{max}}=\frac{r_{\text{max}}}{1-\gamma}</annotation></semantics></math> (Assumption <a href="#S5.Thmassumption2" title="Assumption 5.2 (Bounded Reward). ‣ 5.1 Convergence Analysis ‣ 5 Gradient-Based Weight Optimization ‣ Learning to Optimize Multi-Objective Alignment Through Dynamic Reward Weighting" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.2</span></a>).</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S5.Thmtheorem1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S5.Thmtheorem1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 5.1</span></span><span id="S5.Thmtheorem1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S5.Thmtheorem1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.Thmtheorem1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.Thmtheorem1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Recall the weight update rule defined in Eq. <a href="#S5.E3" title="In 5 Gradient-Based Weight Optimization ‣ Learning to Optimize Multi-Objective Alignment Through Dynamic Reward Weighting" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>, its true weight takes the closed form:</span></p>
<table id="S5.EGx4" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S5.Ex5"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.Ex5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle w_{i}^{(T)}=\frac{w^{(0)}_{i}\exp\big(\sum_{t=1}^{T}\tau^{(t)}I_{i}^{(t)}\big)}{\sum_{k\in[K]}w_{k}^{(0)}\exp\big(\sum_{t=1}^{T}\tau^{(t)}I_{k}^{(t)}\big)},\quad\text{where }\tau^{(t)}=\frac{\eta^{(t)}}{\mu}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo lspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>T</mi></msubsup><mrow><msup><mi>τ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>I</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mrow><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mi>k</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo lspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>T</mi></msubsup><mrow><msup><mi>τ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>I</mi><mi>k</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">where </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>τ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mi>η</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mi>μ</mi></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle w_{i}^{(T)}=\frac{w^{(0)}_{i}\exp\big(\sum_{t=1}^{T}\tau^{(t)}I_{i}^{(t)}\big)}{\sum_{k\in[K]}w_{k}^{(0)}\exp\big(\sum_{t=1}^{T}\tau^{(t)}I_{k}^{(t)}\big)},\quad\text{where }\tau^{(t)}=\frac{\eta^{(t)}}{\mu}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S5.SS1.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S5.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S5.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">The lemma holds when <math id="S5.SS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T=1</annotation></semantics></math>: <math id="S5.SS1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{i}^{(1)}=\frac{w^{(0)}_{i}\exp\big(\tau^{(1)}I_{i}^{(1)}\big)}{\sum_{k\in[K]}w_{k}^{(0)}\exp\big(\tau^{(1)}I_{k}^{(1)}\big)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.710em" minsize="1.710em">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>τ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>I</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo maxsize="1.710em" minsize="1.710em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><msub><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em" stretchy="true">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></msub></mstyle><mrow><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mi>k</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.710em" minsize="1.710em">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>τ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>I</mi><mi>k</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo maxsize="1.710em" minsize="1.710em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{i}^{(1)}=\frac{w^{(0)}_{i}\exp\big(\tau^{(1)}I_{i}^{(1)}\big)}{\sum_{k\in[K]}w_{k}^{(0)}\exp\big(\tau^{(1)}I_{k}^{(1)}\big)}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S5.SS1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">Suppose the lemma holds for all values up to <math id="S5.SS1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T-1</annotation></semantics></math>, for step at <math id="S5.SS1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math>, we have:</span></p>
<table id="S5.EGx5" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S5.Ex6"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.Ex6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle w_{i}^{(T)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle w_{i}^{(T)}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.Ex6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{w_{i}^{(T-1)}\exp(\tau^{(T)}I_{i}^{(T)})}{\sum_{k}w_{k}^{(T-1)}\exp(\tau^{(T)}I_{k}^{(T)})}=\frac{\frac{w^{(0)}_{i}\exp\big(\sum_{t=1}^{T-1}\tau^{(t)}I_{i}^{(t)}\big)}{\sum_{k\in[K]}w_{k}^{(0)}\exp\big(\sum_{t=1}^{T-1}\tau^{(t)}I_{k}^{(t)}\big)}\exp(\tau^{(T)}I_{i}^{(T)})}{\sum_{k}\frac{w^{(0)}_{k}\exp\big(\sum_{t=1}^{T-1}\tau^{(t)}I_{k}^{(t)}\big)}{\sum_{k\in[K]}w_{k}^{(0)}\exp\big(\sum_{t=1}^{T-1}\tau^{(t)}I_{k}^{(t)}\big)}\exp(\tau^{(T)}I_{k}^{(T)})}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>τ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>I</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>k</mi></msub><mrow><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mi>k</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>τ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>I</mi><mi>k</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mfrac><mrow><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.710em" minsize="1.710em">(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><msubsup><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em" stretchy="true">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><msup><mi>τ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>I</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.710em" minsize="1.710em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><msub><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em" stretchy="true">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></msub></mstyle><mrow><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mi>k</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.710em" minsize="1.710em">(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><msubsup><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em" stretchy="true">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><msup><mi>τ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>I</mi><mi>k</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.710em" minsize="1.710em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>τ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>I</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>k</mi></msub><mrow><mfrac><mrow><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mi>k</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.710em" minsize="1.710em">(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><msubsup><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em" stretchy="true">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><msup><mi>τ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>I</mi><mi>k</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.710em" minsize="1.710em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><msub><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em" stretchy="true">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></msub></mstyle><mrow><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mi>k</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.710em" minsize="1.710em">(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><msubsup><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em" stretchy="true">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><msup><mi>τ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>I</mi><mi>k</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.710em" minsize="1.710em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>τ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>I</mi><mi>k</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{w_{i}^{(T-1)}\exp(\tau^{(T)}I_{i}^{(T)})}{\sum_{k}w_{k}^{(T-1)}\exp(\tau^{(T)}I_{k}^{(T)})}=\frac{\frac{w^{(0)}_{i}\exp\big(\sum_{t=1}^{T-1}\tau^{(t)}I_{i}^{(t)}\big)}{\sum_{k\in[K]}w_{k}^{(0)}\exp\big(\sum_{t=1}^{T-1}\tau^{(t)}I_{k}^{(t)}\big)}\exp(\tau^{(T)}I_{i}^{(T)})}{\sum_{k}\frac{w^{(0)}_{k}\exp\big(\sum_{t=1}^{T-1}\tau^{(t)}I_{k}^{(t)}\big)}{\sum_{k\in[K]}w_{k}^{(0)}\exp\big(\sum_{t=1}^{T-1}\tau^{(t)}I_{k}^{(t)}\big)}\exp(\tau^{(T)}I_{k}^{(T)})}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
