</div>
<div id="S5.Thmtheorem2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S5.Thmtheorem2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem 5.2</span></span><span id="S5.Thmtheorem2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S5.Thmtheorem2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.Thmtheorem2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.Thmtheorem2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Suppose Assumptions <a href="#S5.Thmassumption1" title="Assumption 5.1 (Lipschitz Continuity). ‣ 5.1 Convergence Analysis ‣ 5 Gradient-Based Weight Optimization ‣ Learning to Optimize Multi-Objective Alignment Through Dynamic Reward Weighting" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.1</span></a>-<a href="#S5.Thmassumption4" title="Assumption 5.4 (Bounded Policy Gradient). ‣ 5.1 Convergence Analysis ‣ 5 Gradient-Based Weight Optimization ‣ Learning to Optimize Multi-Objective Alignment Through Dynamic Reward Weighting" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.4</span></a> hold and that the step-size sequence of <math id="S5.Thmtheorem2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>τ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau</annotation></semantics></math> converges <math id="S5.Thmtheorem2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\sum_{t=1}\tau^{(t)}-\ell|&lt;\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mo lspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><msup><mi>τ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\sum_{t=1}\tau^{(t)}-\ell|&lt;\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math> for every arbitrarily small positive number <math id="S5.Thmtheorem2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϵ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math>. Then, for every pair of objectives <math id="S5.Thmtheorem2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i,j\in[K]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i,j\in[K]</annotation></semantics></math>, their weight ratio is uniformly bounded: <math id="S5.Thmtheorem2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\smash{w_{i}^{(T)}/w_{j}^{(T)}}=\mathcal{O}(1),\;\forall T\in{\mathbb{N}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>/</mo><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mi>j</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.447em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℕ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\smash{w_{i}^{(T)}/w_{j}^{(T)}}=\mathcal{O}(1),\;\forall T\in{\mathbb{N}}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S5.SS1.3" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S5.SS1.p4" class="ltx_para">
<table id="S5.EGx6" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S5.Ex9"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.Ex9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{w_{i}^{(T)}}{w_{j}^{(T)}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mi>j</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mfrac></mstyle><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{w_{i}^{(T)}}{w_{j}^{(T)}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.Ex9.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{w_{i}^{(0)}\exp\big(\sum_{t=1}^{T}\tau^{(t)}I_{i}^{(t)}\big)}{w_{j}^{(0)}\exp\big(\sum_{t=1}^{T}\tau^{(t)}I_{j}^{(t)}\big)}=\frac{w_{i}^{(0)}}{w_{j}^{(0)}}\exp\Big(\sum_{t=1}^{T}\tau^{(t)}(I_{i}^{(t)}-I_{j}^{(t)})\Big)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo lspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>T</mi></msubsup><mrow><msup><mi>τ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>I</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mi>j</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo lspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>T</mi></msubsup><mrow><msup><mi>τ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>I</mi><mi>j</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mi>j</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>T</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msup><mi>τ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>I</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>I</mi><mi>j</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{w_{i}^{(0)}\exp\big(\sum_{t=1}^{T}\tau^{(t)}I_{i}^{(t)}\big)}{w_{j}^{(0)}\exp\big(\sum_{t=1}^{T}\tau^{(t)}I_{j}^{(t)}\big)}=\frac{w_{i}^{(0)}}{w_{j}^{(0)}}\exp\Big(\sum_{t=1}^{T}\tau^{(t)}(I_{i}^{(t)}-I_{j}^{(t)})\Big)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S5.Ex10"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.Ex10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\frac{w_{i}^{(0)}}{w_{j}^{(0)}}\exp\Big(\sum_{t=1}^{T}\tau^{(t)}2KC^{2}\Big),\quad(I_{i}=\langle\nabla J_{i}(\theta),\sum_{k}\nabla J_{k}(\theta)\rangle\leq KC^{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mi>j</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>T</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msup><mi>τ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>J</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>k</mi></munder></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>J</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\frac{w_{i}^{(0)}}{w_{j}^{(0)}}\exp\Big(\sum_{t=1}^{T}\tau^{(t)}2KC^{2}\Big),\quad(I_{i}=\langle\nabla J_{i}(\theta),\sum_{k}\nabla J_{k}(\theta)\rangle\leq KC^{2})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S5.Ex11"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.Ex11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\frac{w_{i}^{(0)}}{w_{j}^{(0)}}\exp(2KC^{2}\ell)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mi>j</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\frac{w_{i}^{(0)}}{w_{j}^{(0)}}\exp(2KC^{2}\ell)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S5.Ex12"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.Ex12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathcal{O}(1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathcal{O}(1)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.SS1.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS1.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Thmremarkx2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_remark">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmremarkx2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Remark</span></span><span id="Thmremarkx2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmremarkx2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmremarkx2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The ratio <math id="Thmremarkx2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\smash{w_{i}^{(T)}/w_{j}^{(T)}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>/</mo><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mi>j</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\smash{w_{i}^{(T)}/w_{j}^{(T)}}</annotation></semantics></math> measures the cumulative advantage that objective <math id="Thmremarkx2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> has gained over objective <math id="Thmremarkx2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>j</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j</annotation></semantics></math> throughout training, determined by both their initial weights <math id="Thmremarkx2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w^{(0)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>w</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w^{(0)}</annotation></semantics></math> and the accumulated influence across iterations <math id="Thmremarkx2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I^{(t)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>I</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I^{(t)}</annotation></semantics></math>. Intuitively, an objective that is more influential on the gradient update will naturally gain a higher weight relative to a less influential objective.
Keeping this ratio uniformly bounded has two merits. First, it offers numerical stability. A bounded ratio prevents weight collapse or explosion from the exponential update, ensuring that the updated weights <math id="Thmremarkx2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{w}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝒘</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{w}}</annotation></semantics></math> remain properly constrained and ultimately converge to a valid multi‑objective equilibrium. Second, it has practical guidance for hyperparameter selection. Initializing <math id="Thmremarkx2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{w}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝒘</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{w}}</annotation></semantics></math> uniformly and employing a learning rate scheduler in which <math id="Thmremarkx2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta^{(t)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>η</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta^{(t)}</annotation></semantics></math> converges, so that each step updates the weights within safe and predictable bounds.</p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S5.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">5.2 </span>Experiment Setup</h3>

<figure id="alg2" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_float_algorithm ltx_align_middle ltx_align_floatright ltx_framed ltx_framed_top" style="width:218.6pt;"><span class="ltx_rule ltx_figure_panel" style="width:100%;height:1px;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span>
<br class="ltx_break ltx_break">
<div id="alg2.1" class="ltx_listing ltx_listing">
<div id="algx2.l1" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">1:</span>
              
              
            <span id="algx2.l1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Input:</span> Training set <math id="algx2.l1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}_{\text{train}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mtext>train</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}_{\text{train}}</annotation></semantics></math>, initial policy parameters <math id="algx2.l1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>, initial objective weights <math id="algx2.l1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{w}}^{(0)}\!\in\!\mathbb{R}^{K}_{\geq 0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>𝒘</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0.108em" rspace="0.108em">∈</mo><msubsup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi>K</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{w}}^{(0)}\!\in\!\mathbb{R}^{K}_{\geq 0}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="algx2.l2" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">2:</span>
              
              
            <span id="algx2.l2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Hyperparameters:</span> batch size <math id="algx2.l2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>B</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B</annotation></semantics></math>, rollout size <math id="algx2.l2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math>, learning rate <math id="algx2.l2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>η</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta</annotation></semantics></math>, regularization factor <math id="algx2.l2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>μ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu</annotation></semantics></math>, maximum training steps <math id="algx2.l2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="algx2.l3" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">3:</span>
              
              
            <span id="algx2.l3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span> <math id="algx2.l3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\!=\!1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0.108em">=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\!=\!1</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="algx2.l3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">to</span> <math id="algx2.l3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="algx2.l3.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span>

</div>
<div id="algx2.l4" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">4:</span>
              
              
              Sample mini-batch <math id="algx2.l4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}_{b}\subset\mathcal{D}_{\text{train}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi>b</mi></msub><mo>⊂</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mtext>train</mtext></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}_{b}\subset\mathcal{D}_{\text{train}}</annotation></semantics></math> of size <math id="algx2.l4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>B</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="algx2.l5" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">5:</span>
              
              
              <span id="algx2.l5.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for all</span> query <math id="algx2.l5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q\in\mathcal{D}_{b}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi>b</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q\in\mathcal{D}_{b}</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="algx2.l5.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span>

</div>
<div id="algx2.l6" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">6:</span>
              
              
               Sample <math id="algx2.l6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math> answers <math id="algx2.l6.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\{y_{i}\}_{i=1}^{G}\sim\pi_{\theta_{t-1}}(\cdot\mid q)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>G</mi></msubsup><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><msub><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{y_{i}\}_{i=1}^{G}\sim\pi_{\theta_{t-1}}(\cdot\mid q)</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="algx2.l7" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">7:</span>
              
              
               Compute reward vectors <math id="algx2.l7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{{\bm{r}}_{i}\}_{i=1}^{G}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>𝒓</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>G</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{{\bm{r}}_{i}\}_{i=1}^{G}</annotation></semantics></math> for each <math id="algx2.l7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="algx2.l8" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">8:</span>
              
              
              <span id="algx2.l8.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">end</span> <span id="algx2.l8.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span>
</div>
<div id="algx2.l9" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">9:</span>
              
              
              Obtain per-objective gradients <math id="algx2.l9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{\nabla J_{i}(\theta_{t-1},\mathcal{D}_{b})\}_{i=1}^{K}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>J</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi>b</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>K</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\nabla J_{i}(\theta_{t-1},\mathcal{D}_{b})\}_{i=1}^{K}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="algx2.l10" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">10:</span>
              
              
              Compute influence signal <math id="algx2.l10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{I}}^{(t)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝑰</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{I}}^{(t)}</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="algx2.l10.2" class="ltx_text" style="float:right;"><math id="algx2.l10.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\triangleright" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>⊳</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\triangleright</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="algx2.l10.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#008C00;">See Eq. <a href="#S5.E3" title="In 5 Gradient-Based Weight Optimization ‣ Learning to Optimize Multi-Objective Alignment Through Dynamic Reward Weighting" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a></span>
</span>
</div>
<div id="algx2.l11" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">11:</span>
              
              
              <span id="algx2.l11.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Update weights:</span>

</div>
<div id="algx2.l12" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">12:</span>
              
              
                <math id="algx2.l12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{w}}^{(t)}\leftarrow{\bm{w}}^{(t-1)}\odot\exp\!\big(\tfrac{\eta^{(t)}\,{\bm{I}}^{(t)}}{\mu}\big)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>𝒘</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝒘</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊙</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:1.370em;" width="1.370em"><mi>exp</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>η</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝑰</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><mi>μ</mi></mfrac><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{w}}^{(t)}\leftarrow{\bm{w}}^{(t-1)}\odot\exp\!\big(\tfrac{\eta^{(t)}\,{\bm{I}}^{(t)}}{\mu}\big)</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="algx2.l13" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">13:</span>
              
              
                <math id="algx2.l13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{w}}^{(t)}\leftarrow{\bm{w}}^{(t)}\big/\sum_{i}w^{(t)}_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>𝒘</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝒘</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" rspace="0.055em" stretchy="true" symmetric="true">/</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>i</mi></msub><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{w}}^{(t)}\leftarrow{\bm{w}}^{(t)}\big/\sum_{i}w^{(t)}_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="algx2.l14" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">14:</span>
              
              
              Compute scalar rewards <math id="algx2.l14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{\,{\bm{w}}^{(t)\!\top}{\bm{r}}_{i}\,\}_{i=1}^{G}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝒘</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.102em">⊤</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝒓</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>G</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\,{\bm{w}}^{(t)\!\top}{\bm{r}}_{i}\,\}_{i=1}^{G}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="algx2.l15" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">15:</span>
              
              
              Update <math id="algx2.l15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{t-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{t-1}</annotation></semantics></math> via chosen RL objective function <math id="algx2.l15.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J(\theta_{t-1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J(\theta_{t-1})</annotation></semantics></math> using scalarized rewards

</div>
<div id="algx2.l16" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">16:</span>
              
              
            <span id="algx2.l16.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">end</span> <span id="algx2.l16.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span>
</div>
</div>
<br class="ltx_break ltx_break"><span class="ltx_rule" style="width:100%;height:1px;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="alg2.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Algorithm 2</span> </span> Gradient-Based Weight Optimization</figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="S5.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S5.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">As suggested by Theorem <a href="#S5.Thmtheorem2" title="Theorem 5.2. ‣ 5.1 Convergence Analysis ‣ 5 Gradient-Based Weight Optimization ‣ Learning to Optimize Multi-Objective Alignment Through Dynamic Reward Weighting" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.2</span></a>, we initialize the reward weights using a balanced (uniform) setting and use a polynomial learning rate scheduler whose learning rate sequence converges, instead of the constant scheduler used in §<a href="#S4" title="4 Hypervolume-Guided Weight Adaptation ‣ Learning to Optimize Multi-Objective Alignment Through Dynamic Reward Weighting" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>.
To maintain the linearity between the overall reward and the per-objective rewards, we do not add the token-level KL divergence penalty from the reference model in each reward. Furthermore, standard approaches for preference finetuning LLMs with REINFORCE, such as REINFORCE++ <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib19" title="" class="ltx_ref">Hu et al., 2025</a>)</cite>, typically employ clipping mechanisms that render the objective non-differentiable and break the linearity assumptions made in Eq. <a href="#S5.E2" title="In 5 Gradient-Based Weight Optimization ‣ Learning to Optimize Multi-Objective Alignment Through Dynamic Reward Weighting" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>. Therefore, in our experiments, we set both the clip range <math id="S5.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϵ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib34" title="" class="ltx_ref">Schulman et al., 2017</a>)</cite> and dual clip constant <math id="S5.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>c</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c</annotation></semantics></math> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib52" title="" class="ltx_ref">Ye et al., 2020</a>)</cite> high (<math id="S5.SS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon=c=100" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>c</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>100</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon=c=100</annotation></semantics></math>) to practically disable clipping.<span id="footnote4" class="ltx_note ltx_role_footnote"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">4</sup><span class="ltx_note_outer"><span class="ltx_note_content"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">4</sup>
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_note">4</span>
              
              
              
            We also experimented with standard clipping settings (<math id="footnote4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon=0.2,c=3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.2</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon=0.2,c=3</annotation></semantics></math>) and observed that disabling clipping did lead to improved training results.</span></span></span> To improve computational efficiency, we compute gradients only from middle layers, as these layers typically encode the most abstract and generalizable knowledge patterns <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib14" title="" class="ltx_ref">Grosse et al., 2023</a>)</cite>. All other experiment settings follow §<a href="#S4.SS1" title="4.1 Experiment Setup ‣ 4 Hypervolume-Guided Weight Adaptation ‣ Learning to Optimize Multi-Objective Alignment Through Dynamic Reward Weighting" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.1</span></a>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S5.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">5.3 </span>Results</h3>

<figure id="S5.T2" class="ltx_table">
