<span class="ltx_bibblock">In S. Koyejo, S. Mohamed, A. Agarwal, D. Belgrave, K. Cho, and A. Oh (eds.), <em id="bib.bib55.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Advances in Neural Information Processing Systems</em>, volume 35, pp.  38103–38115. Curran Associates, Inc., 2022.

</span>
<span class="ltx_bibblock">URL <a href="https://proceedings.neurips.cc/paper_files/paper/2022/file/f91bd64a3620aad8e70a27ad9cb3ca57-Paper-Conference.pdf" title="" class="ltx_ref ltx_url ltx_font_typewriter">https://proceedings.neurips.cc/paper_files/paper/2022/file/f91bd64a3620aad8e70a27ad9cb3ca57-Paper-Conference.pdf</a>.

</span></li>
      
<li id="bib.bib56" class="ltx_bibitem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_role_refnum ltx_tag_bibitem">Zhou et al. (2024)</span>
<span class="ltx_bibblock">
Zhanhui Zhou, Jie Liu, Jing Shao, Xiangyu Yue, Chao Yang, Wanli Ouyang, and Yu Qiao.

</span>
<span class="ltx_bibblock">Beyond one-preference-fits-all alignment: Multi-objective direct preference optimization.

</span>
<span class="ltx_bibblock">In Lun-Wei Ku, Andre Martins, and Vivek Srikumar (eds.), <em id="bib.bib56.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Findings of the Association for Computational Linguistics: ACL 2024</em>, pp.  10586–10613, Bangkok, Thailand, August 2024. Association for Computational Linguistics.

</span>
<span class="ltx_bibblock">doi: <span class="ltx_ref ltx_nolink ltx_Url ltx_ref_self">10.18653/v1/2024.findings-acl.630</span>.

</span>
<span class="ltx_bibblock">URL <a href="https://aclanthology.org/2024.findings-acl.630/" title="" class="ltx_ref ltx_url ltx_font_typewriter">https://aclanthology.org/2024.findings-acl.630/</a>.

</span></li>
    
</ul>
</section>
<div class="ltx_pagination ltx_role_newpage"></div>
<section id="A1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix A </span>Appendix</h2>

<section id="A1.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.1 </span>Proof for Gradient-Based Weight Optimization</h3>

<div id="A1.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We first write optimizing reward weights <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{w}}\in\mathbb{R}^{K}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝒘</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>K</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{w}}\in\mathbb{R}^{K}</annotation></semantics></math> along the training of the policy model <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>θ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta</annotation></semantics></math> as a bilevel-optimization problem:</p>
<table id="A1.EGx7" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex13"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex13.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle{\bm{w}}\in\argmin_{{\bm{w}}\in\mathbb{R}^{K}}\sum_{i\in[K]}J_{i}(\theta^{\ast}({\bm{w}})),\;\;s.t.\;\theta^{\ast}({\bm{w}})\in\argmin_{\theta}\sum_{i\in[K]}w_{i}J_{i}(\theta)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝒘</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mrow><mi>arg</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>min</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>𝐰</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>K</mi></msup></mrow></msub><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></munder></mstyle><msub><mi>J</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐰</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.727em">,</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">.</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.447em">.</mo><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐰</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msub><mrow><mi>arg</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>min</mi></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msub><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></munder></mstyle><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><msub><mi>J</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle{\bm{w}}\in\argmin_{{\bm{w}}\in\mathbb{R}^{K}}\sum_{i\in[K]}J_{i}(\theta^{\ast}({\bm{w}})),\;\;s.t.\;\theta^{\ast}({\bm{w}})\in\argmin_{\theta}\sum_{i\in[K]}w_{i}J_{i}(\theta).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">The lower-level objective <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta({\bm{w}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒘</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta({\bm{w}})</annotation></semantics></math> is updated using the weights <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{w}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝒘</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{w}}</annotation></semantics></math>, and the higher-level objective <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{w}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝒘</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{w}}</annotation></semantics></math> is found based on the loss function of the updated model. With a greedy approximation of <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\min_{{\bm{w}}}\sum_{i}J_{i}(\theta^{(t)}({\bm{w}}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mrow><mmultiscripts><mo>∑</mo><mi>i</mi><mrow></mrow><mprescripts></mprescripts><mi>𝒘</mi><mrow></mrow></mmultiscripts><mo>⁡</mo><msub><mi>J</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒘</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\min_{{\bm{w}}}\sum_{i}J_{i}(\theta^{(t)}({\bm{w}}))</annotation></semantics></math> (for simplicity, we denote <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta^{(t)}({\bm{w}})=\theta^{(t)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒘</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta^{(t)}({\bm{w}})=\theta^{(t)}</annotation></semantics></math> hereafter), we search for the optimal reward weights <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{w}}^{(t)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝒘</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{w}}^{(t)}</annotation></semantics></math> at step <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math> to minimize the average loss over <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> objectives at step <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t+1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t+1</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="A1.EGx8" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E4"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E4.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\argmin_{{\bm{w}}\in\mathbb{R}^{K}}\bar{J}(\theta^{(t+1)})=\argmin_{{\bm{w}}\in\mathbb{R}^{K}}\sum_{i\in[K]}J_{i}(\theta^{(t+1)})=\argmin_{{\bm{w}}\in\mathbb{R}^{K}}\sum_{i\in[K]}\big[J_{i}(\theta^{(t+1)})-J_{i}(\theta^{(t)})\big]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mi>arg</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>min</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>𝐰</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>K</mi></msup></mrow></msub><mover accent="true"><mi>J</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mi>arg</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>min</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>𝐰</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>K</mi></msup></mrow></msub><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></munder></mstyle><msub><mi>J</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mi>arg</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>min</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>𝐰</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>K</mi></msup></mrow></msub><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><msub><mi>J</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>J</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\argmin_{{\bm{w}}\in\mathbb{R}^{K}}\bar{J}(\theta^{(t+1)})=\argmin_{{\bm{w}}\in\mathbb{R}^{K}}\sum_{i\in[K]}J_{i}(\theta^{(t+1)})=\argmin_{{\bm{w}}\in\mathbb{R}^{K}}\sum_{i\in[K]}\big[J_{i}(\theta^{(t+1)})-J_{i}(\theta^{(t)})\big]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(4)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.p1.3" class="ltx_p">From the first-order Taylor approximation, we have</p>
<table id="A1.EGx9" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex14"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle J_{i}(\theta^{(t+1)})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>J</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle J_{i}(\theta^{(t+1)})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex14.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=J_{i}(\theta^{(t)})+\nabla J_{i}(\theta^{(t)})\cdot(\theta^{(t+1)}-\theta^{(t)})+\mathcal{O}(\|\theta^{(t+1)}-\theta^{(t)}\|)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>J</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>J</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msup><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=J_{i}(\theta^{(t)})+\nabla J_{i}(\theta^{(t)})\cdot(\theta^{(t+1)}-\theta^{(t)})+\mathcal{O}(\|\theta^{(t+1)}-\theta^{(t)}\|)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex15"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex15.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=J_{i}(\theta^{(t)})+\nabla J_{i}(\theta^{(t)})\cdot\Big[-\eta^{(t)}\sum_{i\in[K]}w^{(t)}_{i}\nabla J_{i}(\theta^{(t)})\Big]+\mathcal{O}(\|{\bm{w}}\|)," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>J</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>J</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">[</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><msup><mi>η</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></munder></mstyle><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>J</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">]</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>𝒘</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=J_{i}(\theta^{(t)})+\nabla J_{i}(\theta^{(t)})\cdot\Big[-\eta^{(t)}\sum_{i\in[K]}w^{(t)}_{i}\nabla J_{i}(\theta^{(t)})\Big]+\mathcal{O}(\|{\bm{w}}\|),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.p1.4" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}(\|\theta^{(t+1)}-\theta^{(t)}\|)=\mathcal{O}(\|{\bm{w}}\|)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msup><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>𝒘</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}(\|\theta^{(t+1)}-\theta^{(t)}\|)=\mathcal{O}(\|{\bm{w}}\|)</annotation></semantics></math> as the high-order remainder from Tylor approximation. Therefore, we can write Eq. <a href="#A1.E4" title="In A.1 Proof for Gradient-Based Weight Optimization ‣ Appendix A Appendix ‣ Learning to Optimize Multi-Objective Alignment Through Dynamic Reward Weighting" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a> as:</p>
<table id="A1.EGx10" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex16"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\argmin_{{\bm{w}}\in\mathbb{R}^{K}}\bar{J}(\theta^{(t+1)})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mi>arg</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>min</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>𝐰</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>K</mi></msup></mrow></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>J</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\argmin_{{\bm{w}}\in\mathbb{R}^{K}}\bar{J}(\theta^{(t+1)})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex16.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\argmin_{{\bm{w}}\in\mathbb{R}^{K}}\sum_{i\in[K]}\nabla J_{i}(\theta^{(t)})\cdot\Big[-\eta^{(t)}\sum_{k\in[K]}w^{(t)}_{k}\nabla J_{k}(\theta^{(t)})\Big]+\mathcal{O}(\|{\bm{w}}\|)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mi>arg</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>min</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>𝐰</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>K</mi></msup></mrow></msub><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></munder></mstyle><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>J</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">[</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><msup><mi>η</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></munder></mstyle><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mi>k</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>J</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">]</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>𝐰</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\argmin_{{\bm{w}}\in\mathbb{R}^{K}}\sum_{i\in[K]}\nabla J_{i}(\theta^{(t)})\cdot\Big[-\eta^{(t)}\sum_{k\in[K]}w^{(t)}_{k}\nabla J_{k}(\theta^{(t)})\Big]+\mathcal{O}(\|{\bm{w}}\|)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex17"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex17.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\argmin_{{\bm{w}}\in\mathbb{R}^{K}}-\eta^{(t)}\sum_{i\in[K]}\nabla J_{i}(\theta^{(t)})\cdot\Big[\sum_{k\in[K]}w^{(t)}_{k}\nabla J_{k}(\theta^{(t)})\Big]+\mathcal{O}(\|{\bm{w}}\|)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mi>arg</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>min</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>𝐰</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>K</mi></msup></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>η</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></munder></mstyle><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>J</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">[</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></munder></mstyle><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mi>k</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>J</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">]</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>𝐰</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\argmin_{{\bm{w}}\in\mathbb{R}^{K}}-\eta^{(t)}\sum_{i\in[K]}\nabla J_{i}(\theta^{(t)})\cdot\Big[\sum_{k\in[K]}w^{(t)}_{k}\nabla J_{k}(\theta^{(t)})\Big]+\mathcal{O}(\|{\bm{w}}\|)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex18"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\argmin_{{\bm{w}}\in\mathbb{R}^{K}}-\eta^{(t)}\sum_{i\in[K]}w^{(t)}_{i}\Big[\nabla J_{i}(\theta^{(t)})\cdot\sum_{k\in[K]}\nabla J_{k}(\theta^{(t)})\Big]+\mathcal{O}(\|{\bm{w}}\|)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mi>arg</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>min</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>𝐰</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>K</mi></msup></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>η</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>J</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>J</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>𝐰</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\argmin_{{\bm{w}}\in\mathbb{R}^{K}}-\eta^{(t)}\sum_{i\in[K]}w^{(t)}_{i}\Big[\nabla J_{i}(\theta^{(t)})\cdot\sum_{k\in[K]}\nabla J_{k}(\theta^{(t)})\Big]+\mathcal{O}(\|{\bm{w}}\|)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex19"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\argmin_{{\bm{w}}\in\mathbb{R}^{K}}-\eta^{(t)}\sum_{i\in[K]}w^{(t)}_{i}I_{i}^{(t)}+\mathcal{O}(\|{\bm{w}}\|),\quad\text{where}\;I_{i}^{(t)}\triangleq\langle\nabla J_{i}(\theta^{(t)}),\sum_{k\in[K]}\nabla J_{k}(\theta^{(t)})\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mi>arg</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>min</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>𝐰</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>K</mi></msup></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>η</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>I</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>𝐰</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mtext>where</mtext><mo lspace="0.280em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>I</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo>≜</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>J</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>J</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\argmin_{{\bm{w}}\in\mathbb{R}^{K}}-\eta^{(t)}\sum_{i\in[K]}w^{(t)}_{i}I_{i}^{(t)}+\mathcal{O}(\|{\bm{w}}\|),\quad\text{where}\;I_{i}^{(t)}\triangleq\langle\nabla J_{i}(\theta^{(t)}),\sum_{k\in[K]}\nabla J_{k}(\theta^{(t)})\rangle</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex20"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex20.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\argmin_{{\bm{w}}\in\mathbb{R}^{K}}-\eta^{(t)}\langle{\bm{w}},{\bm{I}}^{(t)}\rangle+\mathcal{O}(\|{\bm{w}}\|),\quad\text{where}\;{\bm{I}}^{(t)}=[I^{(t)}_{1},I^{(t)}_{2},\ldots,I^{(t)}_{K}]." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mi>arg</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>min</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>𝐰</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>K</mi></msup></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>η</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mi>𝐰</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝐈</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>𝐰</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mtext>where</mtext><mo lspace="0.280em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝐈</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>I</mi><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>I</mi><mn>2</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>I</mi><mi>K</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\argmin_{{\bm{w}}\in\mathbb{R}^{K}}-\eta^{(t)}\langle{\bm{w}},{\bm{I}}^{(t)}\rangle+\mathcal{O}(\|{\bm{w}}\|),\quad\text{where}\;{\bm{I}}^{(t)}=[I^{(t)}_{1},I^{(t)}_{2},\ldots,I^{(t)}_{K}].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.p1.5" class="ltx_p">Follow common pratice in mirror descent <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib3" title="" class="ltx_ref">Beck &amp; Teboulle, 2003</a>)</cite>, we estimate <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}(\|{\bm{w}}\|)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>𝒘</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}(\|{\bm{w}}\|)</annotation></semantics></math> by introducing a regularization term with factor <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>μ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu</annotation></semantics></math> via Bregman divergence <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m15" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="D_{h}({\bm{w}}\|{\bm{w}}^{(t-1)})=h({\bm{w}})-h({\bm{w}}^{(t-1)})-\langle\nabla h({\bm{w}}^{(t-1)}),{\bm{w}}-{\bm{w}}^{(t-1)}\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒘</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msup><mi>𝒘</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>h</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒘</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>h</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝒘</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>h</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝒘</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒘</mi><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>𝒘</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{h}({\bm{w}}\|{\bm{w}}^{(t-1)})=h({\bm{w}})-h({\bm{w}}^{(t-1)})-\langle\nabla h({\bm{w}}^{(t-1)}),{\bm{w}}-{\bm{w}}^{(t-1)}\rangle</annotation></semantics></math>, where we employ the entropy function <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h({\bm{w}})=\sum_{i}w_{i}\ln w_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒘</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>i</mi></msub><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>ln</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h({\bm{w}})=\sum_{i}w_{i}\ln w_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>. So the above equation becomes:</p>
<table id="A1.EGx11" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E5"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle{\bm{w}}^{(t)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝒘</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle{\bm{w}}^{(t)}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle:=\argmin_{{\bm{w}}\in\mathbb{R}^{K}}-\eta^{(t)}\langle{\bm{w}},{\bm{I}}^{(t)}\rangle+\mu\Big(h({\bm{w}})-h({\bm{w}}^{(t-1)})-\langle\nabla h({\bm{w}}^{(t-1)}),{\bm{w}}-{\bm{w}}^{(t-1)}\rangle\Big)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mi>arg</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>min</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>𝐰</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>K</mi></msup></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>η</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mi>𝐰</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝐈</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐰</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝐰</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝐰</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>𝐰</mi><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>𝐰</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle:=\argmin_{{\bm{w}}\in\mathbb{R}^{K}}-\eta^{(t)}\langle{\bm{w}},{\bm{I}}^{(t)}\rangle+\mu\Big(h({\bm{w}})-h({\bm{w}}^{(t-1)})-\langle\nabla h({\bm{w}}^{(t-1)}),{\bm{w}}-{\bm{w}}^{(t-1)}\rangle\Big)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(5)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex21"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex21.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\argmin_{{\bm{w}}\in\mathbb{R}^{K}}-\eta^{(t)}\langle{\bm{w}},{\bm{I}}^{(t)}\rangle+\mu\Big(h({\bm{w}})-\langle\nabla h({\bm{w}}^{(t-1)}),{\bm{w}}\rangle\Big)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mi>arg</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>min</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>𝐰</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>K</mi></msup></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>η</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mi>𝐰</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝐈</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐰</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝐰</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐰</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\argmin_{{\bm{w}}\in\mathbb{R}^{K}}-\eta^{(t)}\langle{\bm{w}},{\bm{I}}^{(t)}\rangle+\mu\Big(h({\bm{w}})-\langle\nabla h({\bm{w}}^{(t-1)}),{\bm{w}}\rangle\Big).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.p1.6" class="ltx_p">We then take the derivative of Eq. <a href="#A1.E5" title="In A.1 Proof for Gradient-Based Weight Optimization ‣ Appendix A Appendix ‣ Learning to Optimize Multi-Objective Alignment Through Dynamic Reward Weighting" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>:</p>
<table id="A1.EGx12" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex22"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex22.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\nabla\big(-\eta^{(t)}\langle{\bm{w}},{\bm{I}}^{(t)}\rangle+\mu\big(h({\bm{w}})-\langle\nabla h({\bm{w}}^{(t-1)}),{\bm{w}}\rangle\big)\big)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>∇</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>η</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mi>𝒘</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝑰</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒘</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝒘</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒘</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\nabla\big(-\eta^{(t)}\langle{\bm{w}},{\bm{I}}^{(t)}\rangle+\mu\big(h({\bm{w}})-\langle\nabla h({\bm{w}}^{(t-1)}),{\bm{w}}\rangle\big)\big)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex22.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=0</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex23"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex23.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle-\eta^{(t)}{\bm{I}}^{(t)}+\mu[\ln w+1]_{i}-\mu[\ln w^{(t-1)}+1]_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>η</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝑰</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>ln</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>ln</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msup><mi>w</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle-\eta^{(t)}{\bm{I}}^{(t)}+\mu[\ln w+1]_{i}-\mu[\ln w^{(t-1)}+1]_{i}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex23.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=0</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex24"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex24.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\Rightarrow\ln{\bm{w}}^{(t)}=\ln{\bm{w}}^{(t-1)}+\frac{\eta^{(t)}{\bm{I}}^{(t)}}{\mu}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo stretchy="false">⇒</mo><mrow><mi>ln</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msup><mi>𝒘</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>ln</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msup><mi>𝒘</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>η</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝑰</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><mi>μ</mi></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\Rightarrow\ln{\bm{w}}^{(t)}=\ln{\bm{w}}^{(t-1)}+\frac{\eta^{(t)}{\bm{I}}^{(t)}}{\mu}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright" colspan="2"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.p1.7" class="ltx_p">Therefore, we can get the following update rule for reward weights with normalization:</p>
<table id="A1.EGx13" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E6"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle{\bm{w}}^{(t)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝒘</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle{\bm{w}}^{(t)}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{{\bm{w}}^{(t)}}{\sum_{k}w_{k}^{(t)}},\quad\text{where}\;{\bm{w}}^{(t)}={\bm{w}}^{(t-1)}\odot\exp(\frac{\eta^{(t)}{\bm{I}}^{(t)}}{\mu}),I_{i}^{(t)}=\langle\nabla J_{i}(\theta^{(t)}),\sum_{k\in[K]}\nabla J_{k}(\theta^{(t)})\rangle." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mi>𝒘</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>k</mi></msub><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mi>k</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mtext>where</mtext><mo lspace="0.280em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝒘</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝒘</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊙</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>η</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝑰</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><mi>μ</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>I</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>J</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>J</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{{\bm{w}}^{(t)}}{\sum_{k}w_{k}^{(t)}},\quad\text{where}\;{\bm{w}}^{(t)}={\bm{w}}^{(t-1)}\odot\exp(\frac{\eta^{(t)}{\bm{I}}^{(t)}}{\mu}),I_{i}^{(t)}=\langle\nabla J_{i}(\theta^{(t)}),\sum_{k\in[K]}\nabla J_{k}(\theta^{(t)})\rangle.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(6)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.2 </span>Preliminary Findings</h3>

<figure id="A1.F6" class="ltx_figure"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2509.11452v1/kl_divergence.svg" id="A1.F6.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_square" style="aspect-ratio:548/522;" width="548" height="522"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 6: </span>Pairwise KL divergence trajectories between models trained under different weight configurations. Rows represent the model’s own weight configurations and columns the configuration it is compared against; within each panel, the KL-divergence (y-axis) is plotted over training steps (x-axis).</figcaption>
</figure>
<section id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Accuracy and clarity objectives exhibit synergistic effects while conciseness drives learning orthogonally.</h4>

<div id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">To understand the synergistic or antagonistic effect between different objectives in model training, we analyze pairwise KL divergence trajectories between models trained with different weight configurations: accuracy-focused (<math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.5,0.25,0.25" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0.5</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0.25</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0.25</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.5,0.25,0.25</annotation></semantics></math>), efficiency-focused (<math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.25,0.375,0.375" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0.25</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0.375</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0.375</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.25,0.375,0.375</annotation></semantics></math>), accuracy-only (<math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1,0,0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1,0,0</annotation></semantics></math>), conciseness-only (<math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0,1,0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0,1,0</annotation></semantics></math>), and clarity-only (<math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0,0,1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0,0,1</annotation></semantics></math>). We conduct this study using the Qwen3-8B model trained on the Math500 dataset via GRPO. As shown in <a href="#A1.F6" title="Figure 6 ‣ A.2 Preliminary Findings ‣ Appendix A Appendix ‣ Learning to Optimize Multi-Objective Alignment Through Dynamic Reward Weighting" class="ltx_ref ltx_refmacro_autoref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Figure 6</span></a>, the KL divergence between the accuracy- and clarity-only configurations remains consistently low throughout training, indicating these objectives exhibit strong synergistic effects and induce similar parameter updates. In contrast, models trained with conciseness-only weights diverge significantly from all accuracy- and clarity-only(focused) models, as evidenced by steadily increasing KL divergence over time. This suggests that conciseness applies an orthogonal influence on model optimization, steering parameter updates in a fundamentally different direction compared to accuracy and clarity.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A1.F7" class="ltx_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_3">
<figure id="A1.F7.sf1" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2509.11452v1/accuracy.svg" id="A1.F7.sf1.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:548/358;" width="548" height="358"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">(a) </span>(a) Accuracy</figcaption>
</figure></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_3">
<figure id="A1.F7.sf2" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2509.11452v1/conciseness.svg" id="A1.F7.sf2.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:548/358;" width="548" height="358"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">(b) </span>(b) Conciseness</figcaption>
</figure></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_3">
<figure id="A1.F7.sf3" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2509.11452v1/format.svg" id="A1.F7.sf3.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:548/358;" width="548" height="358"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">(c) </span>(c) Clarity</figcaption>
</figure></div></div>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 7: </span>Validation performance of individual objectives during training. <span id="A1.F7.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Each objective reaches saturation at different training stages.</span> For example, under the conciseness-only weight configuration, the model achieves optimal response brevity at approximately step 165 (<a href="#A1.F7.sf2" title="In Figure 7 ‣ Accuracy and clarity objectives exhibit synergistic effects while conciseness drives learning orthogonally. ‣ A.2 Preliminary Findings ‣ Appendix A Appendix ‣ Learning to Optimize Multi-Objective Alignment Through Dynamic Reward Weighting" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7(b)</span></a>), whereas the clarity-only configuration reaches the best clarity after step 240 (<a href="#A1.F7.sf3" title="In Figure 7 ‣ Accuracy and clarity objectives exhibit synergistic effects while conciseness drives learning orthogonally. ‣ A.2 Preliminary Findings ‣ Appendix A Appendix ‣ Learning to Optimize Multi-Objective Alignment Through Dynamic Reward Weighting" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7(c)</span></a>).</figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Objectives exhibit varying convergence rates.</h4>

<div id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">When training individual objectives, we observe that different objectives reach saturation at different training stages, as illustrated in <a href="#A1.F7" title="Figure 7 ‣ Accuracy and clarity objectives exhibit synergistic effects while conciseness drives learning orthogonally. ‣ A.2 Preliminary Findings ‣ Appendix A Appendix ‣ Learning to Optimize Multi-Objective Alignment Through Dynamic Reward Weighting" class="ltx_ref ltx_refmacro_autoref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Figure 7</span></a>.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.3 </span>Limitations</h3>

<div id="A1.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">While our proposed dynamic reward weighting methods have shown effectiveness on Qwen and DeepSeek models, a key factor is that these models exhibit improvement spaces across all three objectives, enabling our approaches to further optimize training for them. In contrast, for models that inherently struggle to improve all objectives simultaneously, such as Ministral-8B-Instruct <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib28" title="" class="ltx_ref">Mistral AI Team, 2024</a>)</cite> and Llama-3.1-8B-Instruct <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib13" title="" class="ltx_ref">Grattafiori et al., 2024</a>)</cite> that we have tested under the same multi-objective settings, where accuracy consistently declines as responses become shorter, our method is less effective. We think this limitation is unlikely to be addressed via post-training tricks, as it reflects the requirement for models to possess inherent capabilities in each objective, which should ideally be established during pre-training. These observations motivate future works on (1) pre-training strategies that equip models with the capacity to learn and balance diverse objectives, and (2) methods to wisely decide which objectives to prioritize when inherent conflicts exist.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS4" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.4 </span>hypervolume-Guided Reward Adaptation Details</h3>

<div id="A1.SS4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We compute three types of rewards: (1) accuracy reward through exact matching against the provided ground truth, (2) conciseness reward by comparing current response length to the global average response length from previous rollouts, and (3) clarity reward by checking whether responses contain explicit reasoning steps (e.g., “first”, “second”, “third”) according to our pre-defined rules.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS4.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS4.p2.1" class="ltx_p">When training the REINFORCE algorithm with a constant learning rate, we observed significant variation in convergence rates across runs using identical hyperparameters, particularly for the conciseness and clarity objectives. To ensure robust and fair comparisons, we repeated runs three times for all baselines and our proposed approach, reporting results from the run that achieved the fastest convergence in each case. This phenomenon was not observed in other algorithms or training settings, and we leave its investigation to future works.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS4.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS4.p3.1" class="ltx_p">We also observed that zero reward would result in increased response length and degraded performance in both accuracy and formatting, which is likely due to the entropy penalty dominating the gradient updates. To mitigate this issue, we build a minimum threshold of <math id="A1.SS4.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{\text{pareto}}=0.5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mtext>pareto</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0.5</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{\text{pareto}}=0.5</annotation></semantics></math> in Eq. <a href="#S4.E1" title="In 4 Hypervolume-Guided Weight Adaptation ‣ Learning to Optimize Multi-Objective Alignment Through Dynamic Reward Weighting" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> even when the current checkpoint is Pareto dominated (i.e., <math id="A1.SS4.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta\text{HV}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext>HV</mtext></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta\text{HV}=0</annotation></semantics></math>).</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS5" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.5 </span>Hyperparameters</h3>

<figure id="A1.T4" class="ltx_table">
